WEBVTT

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.110
In this wide world

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.290
People you're meant to meet can be seen

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.860
Beyond the window, beyond the rainbow

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.490
I think you're aware of them

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:45.610
Take off that restrictive weight

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.580
Let your feelings go

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:55.880
Now keep your ears open and wait for that time

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.650
Awaken now

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:11.930
Cherish the little dream you've
drawn in the vast sky

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:19.210
If you do, you can always become happy

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:21.980
It's certain

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:26.350
Woh woh

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:35.420
People live their lives in search of happiness.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:42.390
Goddesses impart just a little bit
of happiness to certain people.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:49.490
And the goddesses also find their own salvation
through that special person's smile.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:56.740
This is the tale of a man who accepted
the love of one such goddess.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:02.750
Ah! I Wish...           Once More!

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.130
I have returned at last...

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:14.630
I have returned at last...

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:14.920
TARIKI HONGANTEMPLE

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:20.300
It has already been eleven months and
three days since I once again departed

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.700
to pursue my ascetic training.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:28.740
It was all so that I might be one who brings
happiness unto people as Lady Belldandy does.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:34.750
With that thought, I continued on my journey,
seeking out song that cleanses people's hearts.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:38.240
I went to any and every place where
songs could be found.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:43.560
Today, I return to report what
my training has yielded.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.220
My word, the place is in excellent shape!

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.430
I'm sure the temple is glad...

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:53.900
Well, I guess I'll go say hello to everyone.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:57.970
What's going on here?!

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:02.570
There is NO way I am going to
put up with this today!

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:04.450
What the heck did I do?

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.680
Gimme a break!
What the heck did I do?

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:06.370
Gimme a break!

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.020
You're always making fun of my inventions!

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.390
I'm plenty helpful to Big Sister!

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.230
Quarreling like this before the image
of Buddha is inexcusable!

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.590
Well, she's the one that spilled the precious

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.760
"One Glance and Your Heart is Mine"
potion that I had mixed up!

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:22.800
What's your problem?!

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.330
Who's the one who wrecked my lawn mower
by dropping depth charges on it?!

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:29.340
I told you to stop your bickering!

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.840
What you two lack is love!

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.810
Hear my song of love, which I
shall now sing for you!

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:34.910
Summon lightning bolt!
Hear my song of love, which I
shall now sing for you!

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:35.530
Summon lightning bolt!

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.110
Banpei SCAD, go!

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:40.810
Cut it out already!

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:44.120
Sheesh, what are ranting and
raving to yourself over?

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.760
Yeah! You've been raising quite
a racket in our garden!

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.060
Who do you think you are, little girl?!
This is MY temple!

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.830
And your insolent manner will lead
your heart to corruption.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.830
Now, hear my song!

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.660
Then cast aside all doubt, and come to my...

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.900
I have much to learn...

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:13.010
I cannot yet face Lady Belldandy
after an incident like this!

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.120
It is time for me to resume
my spiritual training!

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.390
Some acquaintance of Big Sister's?

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.410
Dunno.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:21.120
Here you go!

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.180
Thanks.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:25.660
That was a huge crash earlier.
You sure everything's okay?

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.030
Probably just Urd and Skuld fighting again...

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:31.690
They take sibling arguments
to a whole new level!

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:35.040
It's because they get along so well.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.660
Just like you and Keiichi!

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.410
What was that for, Kei-chan?

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:44.150
You know, there simply aren't many sisters like
me, who care so deeply for their older brothers!

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.950
If that's true, then I'd like you to
keep your distance a little more.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:50.690
Now, you wouldn't be thinking that
my being here is keeping you two

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.650
from being ALL alone together, would you?

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:56.780
I think the more the merrier.

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:01.380
I pity you, Kei-chan.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.650
Keiichi?

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.640
You know, it's been almost a year since
you came to this old temple.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:11.540
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:14.340
It's almost hard to believe it has
already been so long

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.510
since Keiichi and I made our
contract with each other.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:17.910
Contract?!

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.180
Well, now!

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:25.250
So are there monetary issues that
keep you two together then?

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.420
I think you're getting the wrong idea here.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:31.830
That's right. We are bound
by a heavenly contract.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.890
Belldandy, you're a weirdo.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.930
Due to the work of Belldandy
and her companions,

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:40.570
the Ultimate Destruction Program
was terminated.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:43.600
As for the data that was lost in
the sealing of the Gate of the Netherworld,

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:47.130
all has returned to normal, save for five
percent, which was unrecoverable.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.850
My word. What a troublesome program
we were stuck with...

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.250
Almighty?

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:54.850
What is it?

00:05:54.850 --> 00:06:00.150
In this case, the Goddess Help Line registration
file was among the areas that were damaged.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:05.650
Will Belldandy be able to remain
on the Earth as she is now?

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:08.060
You are referring to her contract?

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:09.030
Yes.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:11.370
Because of the Lord of Terror fiasco,

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.040
there is a limit to the time one can
spend on the surface world.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.710
Eventually, she will have to return
to her station here.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.380
I will contact him.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.000
You may go.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:23.570
My lord.

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:32.150
We've got Professor Kasahara's
lecture today, right?

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:33.980
I'm looking forward to it.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.090
Oh, you guys are going out?

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:40.090
Yeah, we're going to class.

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:42.060
Ooh! I'll come, too!

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:50.340
Morisato residence.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.460
Huh?!

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.810
What do you mean it's "you"?
Who is this?

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.180
HUH?!

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.280
THE ALMIGHTY?!

00:06:58.280 --> 00:06:59.370
What?!

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.580
Are you party to the contract?

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.880
Yes!

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:05.850
The call is for Keiichi?!

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:06.880
Why?

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:11.930
Regarding your contract, I am sorry,
but as it was destroyed,

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:16.130
I cannot allow the goddesses to stay
on Earth for an extended period.

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:18.630
The Lord of Terror incident was
a burden to you,

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:21.140
so I have decided to grant
a short moratorium.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:25.440
I ask that you find some sense
of closure, if anything.

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:29.600
That's not such an easy thing
to deal with out of the blue...

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.050
Even if it was the Lord of Terror's fault,

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:36.140
they were still the ones who deleted all
the data, so Keiichi's not to blame at all!

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:40.990
Yeah, but since the Almighty, Himself, contacted
me directly, there's not much I can do...

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:43.150
What are we gonna do, Big Sister?

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:47.130
It's not like they've determined that
we need to return immediately.

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:51.470
Plus, I'm not the only helper
goddess working in Heaven,

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:56.370
so I don't think they'll be
shorthanded anytime soon.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:58.030
Is that right...

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:03.910
Still, though... I don't get why Keiichi's wish
would be the only one that got deleted.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:06.180
Makes me wonder if a certain someone
erased a certain something

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:07.520
along with the Lord of Terror?

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:10.180
What is your problem?!
Are you saying I'M to blame?!

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:12.090
Hey, who's the one that got
possessed by the Great Lord,

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.550
and seemed to enjoy destroying
the whole town so much?

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:17.890
Now there's something I'd sure
like to have deleted.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.690
Well, it's not going away!

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.730
I have found some fragments,

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:25.290
but the damage to the essential
voice data is in bad shape.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:29.740
If I can restore that, it may be
possible to play it back.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:34.140
Then the contractor's pact is necessary?

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:35.270
Yes.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.780
Contact him.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:39.080
Understood.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:42.280
Hello?

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:45.080
What? You say you can recover it?!

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:52.890
It means they're going to reenter Keiichi's
wish into the system and restore his file.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:56.100
You're okay doing that, right, Keiichi?

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.730
Yeah, it's fine!

00:08:57.730 --> 00:08:59.030
Are you ready?

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:01.870
What are you so tense for?

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:03.500
This should be simple.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:05.360
Uh... right.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.310
Stay cool...

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:08.780
Gotta stay cool!

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.010
Voice monitoring, check.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.780
Please go ahead.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:15.350
Sure. Uhhh. Uh. Uhh Ah...

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:16.720
Hurry up!
Sure. Uhhh. Uh. Uhh Ah...

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:17.320
Hurry up!

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.680
All right!

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:25.120
I'd like a goddess like you to
always stay by my side.

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:27.750
That should be okay, right?

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:32.270
The system was unable recognize that.
Please repeat.

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:36.290
I'd like a goddess like you to always
stay by my side! Isn't that it?!

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:40.740
Unable to recognize. It is possible you
have mistaken one or more words.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.800
That can't be...

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:46.510
How could you forget your own wish?!

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:48.810
I'm certain that's what I said!

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:52.820
I wish I could live with a goddess like you!

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.220
I wish I had a girlfriend like you!

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:55.760
I sure wish I could eat some
of your homemade food!

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:58.050
Do you want to go visit the
museum with me?!

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:04.030
I'm impressed that you can say that much.

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:05.660
I'm getting an error message.

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:10.560
I wonder if it's just that the system is so
damaged that they can't do voice recognition.

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:15.610
Actually, Belldandy... don't you already
have the passphrase recorded?

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:16.840
Yes...

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:18.980
So what about it?

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:25.150
It's protected, so I can't say
the code myself...

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:29.550
It's wrong.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:32.430
There's this Memory Restoration Hammer.

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:34.930
And Lady Urd's Special Memory
Restoration Extract.

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:37.030
Which would you prefer?

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.330
W-Wait! I'm trying to remember it now!

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:41.340
Then let us help you speed up the process.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.940
Yeah! You're the lowest of the low to have
forgotten your contract with Big Sister!

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:47.070
Maybe getting hit by a few depth charges
would help you more?

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:49.280
Or Banpei's Special Attack!

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.710
Listen, before you do any of that...

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.840
Enough of this!

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:57.980
Try to put yourselves in Keiichi's place!

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.350
Keiichi, do you want to go to campus?

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:04.790
You're going to school at a time like this?!

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:08.160
In times like this, a change
of pace is in order.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.660
Isn't that right, Keiichi?

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:13.770
Yeah.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:28.550
I think it's best not to worry
about it that much.

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:31.990
It's not your fault that the contract was deleted.

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:32.920
Given that...
It's not your fault that the contract was deleted.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:33.050
Given that...

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:34.760
Given that...
But even so...

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:39.530
that wish is the only reason we can
come to class together like this

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:42.390
and work together and all that stuff...

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:47.260
Thanks to your wish we can be
together like this, can't we?

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:51.510
Yeah, so the fact that I forgot the wish means...

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:53.800
What did you forget?

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:55.710
Seniors!

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:57.910
Umm... it's just, uh, that I don't know

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:00.350
the combustion rate in this
internal combustion engine!

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:02.080
What did you say?!

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:04.820
You're in the Auto Club, and you
don't know something like that?!

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:05.590
You're a disgrace to the Auto Club!
You're in the Auto Club, and you
don't know something like that?!

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:06.320
You're a disgrace to the Auto Club!

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:08.120
You oughta be ashamed of yourself!

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:10.790
Then we'll just give you some
intensive study now!

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.760
Get ready.

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:15.230
Uh, but I've got work after this!

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:27.740
I'm sorry, but Keiichi and I have
work now, so please pardon us.

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:30.580
Come on, Keiichi, let's go.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:36.680
You've returned?

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:40.390
Well, I won't be able to solve anything
down on the surface world.

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:44.360
Can't you get into the main system
and retrieve the code?

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.420
That would constitute a very serious crime!

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.560
Don't be so rash.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.970
We're already pushing it with
what we're doing now.

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:54.160
I came back here knowing
I'd be pushing things.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:56.240
Welcome!

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:56.670
Fried chicken
Green Tea Boxed Lunch

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:57.070
Fried chicken
Green Tea Boxed Lunch

00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:59.540
So you'd like me to warm
this up for you, right?

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:01.340
No problem!

00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:12.280
Here you go! Thanks for your patience!

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:14.520
Thank you very much!

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:18.920
Why did you do that?

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:23.490
It's because you said you wanted us
to be alone together.

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:29.500
We might not have very much time
left together either...

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:32.470
When I thought about that, I just...

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:34.000
I see.

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:38.410
TARIKI HONGANTEMPLE

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:39.910
We're back.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:41.940
What's all this?!

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:44.440
It's going into Skuld's room...

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:47.560
If this is how it's gonna be, then
I'll hack into the main bank

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:50.460
and swipe the code from Big Sister's file!

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:54.530
Once my "Hello, Hackman" is complete,
nothing will be impossible!

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:56.400
Why's she messing around with that stuff?

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:59.420
I'm sure it's because she's
concerned for you.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.840
I might even be able to get Big Sister to
become disgusted with that slob, Keiichi,

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:08.910
and praise me and say, "Oh, what a
wonderful job you've done, Skuld!"

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.340
So concerned...

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:12.810
All right, Skuld, time to give it one last push!

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:15.880
Here you go.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:17.440
Thanks.

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:24.830
What's wrong?

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:27.230
Uh, nothing...

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:29.560
Well, thanks for the meal!

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:35.160
She always put a smile on for me,

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:40.500
so I guess I'll have to reciprocate, won't I?

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:47.580
Because her smile is what I want to see!

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:55.150
Especially now...

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:01.520
Belldandy?

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:03.060
Yes?

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:08.530
It's Sunday, and it's a nice day out, too,
so do you want to go out with me?

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:11.030
Where are you going?

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:14.980
Um, well... I haven't really decided yet...

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:17.770
I figured maybe we could go on a date.

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:22.100
Because I want to treasure the rest of
the time we spend together.

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:25.320
Sure!

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:28.760
Okay, then I'll make some lunch for us!

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:29.720
Okay.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:34.830
Well, this is what I wanted,

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:38.990
but suddenly calling this a date
has made me pretty nervous...

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.500
Do I really have that kind of courage?

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:45.870
No... I decided that this was a date.

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:47.340
That much, at least...

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:48.970
Is something the matter?

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.210
No, nothing at all!

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:53.210
Well, shall we get going then?

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:54.340
Keiichi?

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:57.450
Keiichi!

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:03.220
This is the first time you've invited
me out on an actual date.

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:07.780
So let's have a wonderful day!

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:16.060
Well, I guess it's pointless to force it.

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:19.270
Oh, brother...

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:22.610
Could they at least hold each other's hands?

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:25.180
Well... Are you sure it's okay
to be doing this?

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:26.540
It's fine!

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:30.540
Since all we're doing here is gathering
Keiichi's voice data...

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.640
What a beautiful view!

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:39.490
Belldandy looks best when she's smiling.

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:42.850
She's enjoying herself so much, too...

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:45.860
Keiichi!

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.740
Thanks, that'll be 600 yen, please.

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:50.730
Crap!

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:56.540
I used up all of last month's
earnings on gas for today!

00:16:56.710 --> 00:17:00.010
Keiichi, you can use this if you don't mind.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.450
No, I couldn't!
The guy's supposed to pay for stuff!

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:06.890
I haven't used one bit of my recent earnings,

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:09.690
so why don't you let me buy this time?

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:10.320
Thank you!

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:11.330
Thank you!
Well, I'll take you up on it then.

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:12.730
Well, I'll take you up on it then.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:13.750
Sure!

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:16.190
Over here!

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:17.830
Wait up!

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:20.770
Here you go.

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:25.000
It's nice to eat lunch out in a place
like this, too, isn't it?

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.370
Is it good?

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:28.940
Mmm, it's delicious.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:30.310
Great!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.980
You having fun?

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:35.540
I am.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:40.890
It would have been nice to have had lots
more dates like this, huh?

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:42.590
You're right.

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:45.230
How about we go up to the
observation deck next?

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:47.230
That'll be an even nicer view.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:49.530
Sure. Let's go!

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:57.660
Wonder if we could at least
hold hands or something...

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:00.360
Keiichi!

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:02.930
What's wrong?

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:05.240
Sorry! I'm coming!

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:12.950
Keiichi!

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:19.790
Dance, Spirits, gather at my command,
and save him!

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:28.600
Keiichi!

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:32.540
Thanks. You saved me there.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:35.130
You had me so scared for a minute.

00:18:38.150 --> 00:18:40.170
What was THAT just now?!

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:43.280
It was n-nothing at all!

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:45.950
Excuse us! Let's go, Belldandy!

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:47.250
A-All right!

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:54.220
You've been so much help
to me all this time...

00:18:54.630 --> 00:19:01.260
I haven't really done anything for you
in return, though, even today...

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:03.900
It's not like that at all.

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:08.200
You have always kept me in mind.

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:16.320
Enough to make me forget I am here under a
contract from the Goddess Assistance Agency.

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:22.220
You know, I want to be with you forever.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:24.790
I feel the same.

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:31.130
So... as long as we feel this way,
we'll be able to be together again.

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:35.260
I think even if you do go back,
we'll be able to meet again some day.

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:38.400
I... think so.

00:19:38.710 --> 00:19:41.670
This doesn't mean we'll never
be able to see each other again.

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:52.080
If you have a need for me, I think my
feelings will also reach you.

00:19:53.150 --> 00:19:56.850
Because my feelings will never change.

00:19:58.060 --> 00:19:59.560
Belldandy?

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:00.460
Yes?

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:03.960
I've always wished...

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:09.460
for a goddess like you to
always stay by my side.

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:11.690
Keiichi...

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:20.980
It's reacting!

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:46.170
See, it's just like I said!

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:49.710
We did it! Voice recognition!

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:52.380
Voice data confirmed.
Contract approved.

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:54.180
We did it!

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:57.120
Your snooping did just the trick, Urd!

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:00.210
Thanks for the help.

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:04.790
There's no need for thanks.
After all, I have done nothing here.

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:08.690
And you did even less, Urd.

00:21:09.230 --> 00:21:10.560
What was that?

00:21:10.560 --> 00:21:12.830
N-Nothing! I was only joking!

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:16.190
Well, I guess I'll be heading back
to the surface world then.

00:21:18.470 --> 00:21:20.000
Keiichi...

00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:23.340
Here's to our continued life together!

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:26.070
Belldandy...

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:28.710
You bet.

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:31.880
Here's to it.

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:42.050
I will always be by your side.

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:44.860
Uh... Yeah.

00:21:50.840 --> 00:21:54.740
Coming back to this temple really
is relaxing, isn't it?

00:21:54.740 --> 00:21:58.480
That's because all the time we've
spent here is so dear to us.

00:21:58.480 --> 00:22:01.970
As well as the time we will
spend here, right?

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:04.110
Belldandy...

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:08.820
How could you go and make a waste of
the machine I made just for you?!

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:10.860
Even Heaven itself can't take its
eyes off you for a second,

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:11.630
I hope that their relationship will
develop a little bit now.
Even Heaven itself can't take its
